1
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:37,660
- Look out! - Fire! Fire!

2
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:05,920
A band of 20 men, maybe less.

3
00:03:06,370 --> 00:03:08,550
They were in and out before anyone spotted them.

4
00:03:08,550 --> 00:03:10,480
Burnt our food stores to the ground,

5
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:12,540
all our siege weapons destroyed.

6
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:15,060
- Dozens of tents were-- - Horses?

7
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:17,490
We're still getting a count, but hundreds are dead.

8
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:19,220
20 men rode into our camp

9
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:21,210
without a single guard sounding the alarm?

10
00:03:21,210 --> 00:03:23,630
The northerners know more about their land than we ever will.

11
00:03:23,630 --> 00:03:24,950
Put last night's guards in chains.

12
00:03:24,950 --> 00:03:27,100
Either they fell asleep or they conspired with the enemy.

13
00:03:27,110 --> 00:03:29,950
- Find out the truth and then hang them. - Your Grace.

14
00:03:30,670 --> 00:03:34,120
Unless there's a thaw, we can't press forward to Winterfell

15
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:36,790
and we don't have enough food to get us back to Castle Black.

16
00:03:36,790 --> 00:03:38,550
We're not returning to Castle Black.

17
00:03:38,550 --> 00:03:39,520
Forgive me, Your Grace,

18
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:41,930
I never claimed to be an expert in military matters,

19
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:45,330
but if we can't march forward and we won't march back...

20
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:01,150
Have the dead horses butchered for meat.

21
00:04:42,150 --> 00:04:43,450
Halt!

22
00:04:44,630 --> 00:04:46,280
Halt!

23
00:04:49,810 --> 00:04:51,770
There it is!

24
00:05:32,190 --> 00:05:33,930
Open the gates.

25
00:05:50,130 --> 00:05:51,640
It was a failure.

26
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:53,750
It wasn't.

27
00:05:55,020 --> 00:05:56,930
I went to save them. I failed.

28
00:05:58,990 --> 00:06:00,520
You didn't fail him.

29
00:06:01,410 --> 00:06:02,450
Or him.

30
00:06:03,010 --> 00:06:04,450
Or her.

31
00:06:05,410 --> 00:06:08,680
Every one of them is alive because of you and no one else.

32
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:12,480
I don't think that fact's lost on them.

33
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:09,220
You have a good heart, Jon Snow.

34
00:07:10,170 --> 00:07:11,950
It'll get us all killed.

35
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,120
Out of my way.

36
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:48,410
You sent for me, Your Grace?

37
00:07:48,410 --> 00:07:50,620
Find some healthy horses and a few knights to guard you.

38
00:07:50,620 --> 00:07:52,320
I'm sending you back to Castle Black.

39
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:54,780
Tell the Lord Commander his king commands him

40
00:07:54,780 --> 00:07:57,310
to send food, supplies, fresh horses.

41
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:59,210
In return, when I take the throne,

42
00:07:59,210 --> 00:08:02,180
I'll make sure the Night's Watch has all the men it requires.

43
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:05,200
He can guard all 19 castles on the Wall if he so wishes.

44
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:10,640
Your Grace, you named me your Hand.

45
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:12,190
Yes.

46
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:14,290
The King's Hand should never abandon the king,

47
00:08:14,290 --> 00:08:15,740
especially in time of war.

48
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:17,910
You're not abandoning me. You're obeying a command.

49
00:08:17,910 --> 00:08:20,320
A boy with a scroll could deliver this message.

50
00:08:20,320 --> 00:08:22,490
And if Jon Snow refuses the boy with the scroll,

51
00:08:22,490 --> 00:08:24,030
what does the boy say?

52
00:08:24,490 --> 00:08:26,870
I didn't name you Hand for your expertise in military matters.

53
00:08:26,870 --> 00:08:29,290
Ride for Castle Black. Don't come back empty-handed.

54
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:38,570
Your Grace, perhaps Queen Selyse

55
00:08:38,570 --> 00:08:40,350
and Princess Shireen could accompany me.

56
00:08:40,350 --> 00:08:42,070
My family stays with me.

57
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:44,760
At least let me take Shireen.

58
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:47,100
A siege is no place for a little girl.

59
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:48,900
My family stays with me.

60
00:09:25,750 --> 00:09:26,990
What's this one now?

61
00:09:26,990 --> 00:09:29,560
"The Dance of Dragons: A True Telling"

62
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:31,120
by Grand Maester Munkun.

63
00:09:31,270 --> 00:09:33,280
Now that sounds like a proper story.

64
00:09:34,190 --> 00:09:36,550
Ser Byron Swann wanted to kill the dragon Vhagar.

65
00:09:36,980 --> 00:09:39,660
He polished his shield for a week so that it was like a mirror.

66
00:09:39,660 --> 00:09:41,910
And he crouched behind it and crept forward,

67
00:09:41,910 --> 00:09:44,080
hoping the dragon would only see its own reflection.

68
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:47,420
But the dragon saw a dumb man holding a mirrored shield.

69
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:49,150
And burnt him to a crisp.

70
00:09:49,770 --> 00:09:53,830
Thus ending the dragon-slaying career of Ser Byron Swann.

71
00:09:57,630 --> 00:09:59,670
I made you something, Princess.

72
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:07,710
Do you like it?

73
00:10:07,710 --> 00:10:08,900
He's beautiful.

74
00:10:10,370 --> 00:10:12,230
- Thank you. - You're very welcome.

75
00:10:12,540 --> 00:10:15,200
Will you make me a doe, too? So that he can have company?

76
00:10:15,210 --> 00:10:16,330
Of course I will.

77
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:20,050
But why am I getting a present?

78
00:10:21,450 --> 00:10:22,950
Because you deserve it.

79
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:27,790
My son was always on me, trying to teach me to read.

80
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:30,170
Gods, I was stubborn about it.

81
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:33,510
Made it this far without reading.

82
00:10:33,510 --> 00:10:35,500
Seemed to me I could make it to the grave.

83
00:10:38,140 --> 00:10:39,540
Wish I'd listened to him.

84
00:10:41,810 --> 00:10:44,090
This is my own poor way of saying thank you.

85
00:10:47,820 --> 00:10:49,660
For teaching me to be a grown-up.

86
00:10:52,810 --> 00:10:54,780
I'll be gone for a few days, Princess.

87
00:10:55,790 --> 00:10:58,390
I want to hear all about "The Dance of Dragons" when I'm back.

88
00:10:58,580 --> 00:11:00,160
You'll read it yourself.

89
00:11:21,820 --> 00:11:23,100
Prince Doran.

90
00:11:23,150 --> 00:11:25,950
Forgive us. We started without you.

91
00:11:26,770 --> 00:11:28,670
Please, sit.

92
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:31,010
Princess Myrcella.

93
00:11:31,890 --> 00:11:33,010
Uncle.

94
00:11:33,410 --> 00:11:34,820
What a lovely dress.

95
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:37,070
- You don't like it? - You must be cold.

96
00:11:37,070 --> 00:11:40,180
Not at all. The Dornish climate agrees with me.

97
00:11:42,070 --> 00:11:43,790
Prince Trystane.

98
00:11:46,890 --> 00:11:48,230
How's your jaw?

99
00:11:49,070 --> 00:11:50,460
A fleabite.

100
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:52,250
What are you doing in Dorne?

101
00:11:52,250 --> 00:11:55,060
Looking after the safety of my niece, the Princess Myrcella.

102
00:11:55,060 --> 00:11:58,190
And rather than send a raven or speak to me directly,

103
00:11:58,190 --> 00:12:00,380
you decided to enter my country in secret

104
00:12:00,380 --> 00:12:02,370
and abduct our guest by force?

105
00:12:02,370 --> 00:12:04,500
We received a threatening message.

106
00:12:05,730 --> 00:12:08,960
The princess's necklace in the jaws of a viper.

107
00:12:09,990 --> 00:12:12,100
That necklace was stolen from my room.

108
00:12:17,910 --> 00:12:20,530
Oh, excellent.

109
00:12:20,960 --> 00:12:22,610
A last meal before the beheading?

110
00:12:22,750 --> 00:12:24,330
Oh, I can't behead you.

111
00:12:24,900 --> 00:12:26,380
Many in Dorne want war.

112
00:12:27,150 --> 00:12:28,450
But I've seen war.

113
00:12:29,260 --> 00:12:31,770
I've seen the bodies piled on the battlefields.

114
00:12:32,230 --> 00:12:35,300
I've seen the orphans starving in the cities.

115
00:12:35,490 --> 00:12:37,480
I don't want to lead my people into that hell.

116
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:40,380
No, you want to break bread with the Lannisters.

117
00:12:40,380 --> 00:12:42,810
And that is precisely what we are doing.

118
00:12:44,450 --> 00:12:48,280
Let us drink to Tommen, the First of His Name,

119
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:50,600
King of the Andals and the First Men,

120
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:52,580
Lord of the Seven Kingdoms.

121
00:13:10,260 --> 00:13:12,530
King Tommen insists

122
00:13:12,860 --> 00:13:15,040
on his sister's return to the capital?

123
00:13:16,790 --> 00:13:18,340
I'm afraid he does.

124
00:13:20,020 --> 00:13:22,490
I cannot disobey my king's command.

125
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:25,480
She will return with you to King's Landing.

126
00:13:25,620 --> 00:13:29,310
And my son Prince Trystane will accompany you both.

127
00:13:29,310 --> 00:13:32,410
If the alliance between the Iron Throne and Dorne is to continue,

128
00:13:32,860 --> 00:13:35,060
their engagement must stand.

129
00:13:35,710 --> 00:13:37,030
I accept.

130
00:13:37,030 --> 00:13:39,080
One more thing. My brother was named

131
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:41,590
to the small council before his death.

132
00:13:41,990 --> 00:13:45,940
Your father understood the importance of keeping Dorne in the fold.

133
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:47,030
With Oberyn gone,

134
00:13:47,030 --> 00:13:49,620
Trystane will take his place on the small council.

135
00:13:50,260 --> 00:13:51,750
You have my word.

136
00:13:51,750 --> 00:13:54,100
The word of a kingslayer.

137
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:59,650
No wonder you can't stand. You have no spine.

138
00:14:00,910 --> 00:14:02,840
You are mother to four of my nieces,

139
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:04,640
girls I love very much.

140
00:14:04,650 --> 00:14:07,560
For their sake, I hope you live a long and happy life.

141
00:14:07,560 --> 00:14:10,500
Speak to me that way again, and you won't.

142
00:14:17,730 --> 00:14:21,400
May I inquire as to the fate of my man Bronn?

143
00:14:21,610 --> 00:14:24,110
Tell me, Ser Jaime, in King's Landing,

144
00:14:24,610 --> 00:14:27,910
how do they punish a commoner who strikes a prince?

145
00:14:27,910 --> 00:14:29,850
He said it was just a fleabite.

146
00:14:32,140 --> 00:14:33,510
The fault is mine.

147
00:14:33,790 --> 00:14:36,280
Bronn is merely a soldier following my orders.

148
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:38,400
If anyone should be punished, it's me.

149
00:14:39,460 --> 00:14:42,780
Prince Trystane must learn judgment if he is to rule one day.

150
00:14:42,780 --> 00:14:44,250
I'll let him decide.

151
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:52,160
I have learned the value of mercy from my father.

152
00:14:52,190 --> 00:14:55,240
- I'll set your man free. - You're a good man.

153
00:14:55,710 --> 00:14:57,290
On one condition.

154
00:15:05,340 --> 00:15:07,910
Why do we play? I'm better than you.

155
00:15:07,910 --> 00:15:10,500
I'll always be better than you.

156
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:13,280
Have I ever missed once?

157
00:15:13,880 --> 00:15:16,120
I don't think I have. I can't recall.

158
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:18,600
You must love humiliation. Or pain.

159
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:22,290
Which do you love most, humiliation or pain?

160
00:15:24,230 --> 00:15:25,890
That one hurt, didn't it?

161
00:15:26,630 --> 00:15:27,950
You going to cry?

162
00:15:28,780 --> 00:15:30,190
Give up, little sister.

163
00:15:30,480 --> 00:15:32,950
- You're going to miss. - Oh, I never miss.

164
00:15:32,950 --> 00:15:35,450
You will. You're thinking too much.

165
00:15:36,030 --> 00:15:39,150
Now you're nervous. What if she's right?

166
00:15:42,730 --> 00:15:45,290
- Luck. - Now it's my turn.

167
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:46,700
You're too slow.

168
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:48,730
You've always been too slow.

169
00:16:05,310 --> 00:16:07,420
Am I gonna be happy at the end of this walk?

170
00:16:07,420 --> 00:16:09,340
You'll find out very soon.

171
00:16:12,510 --> 00:16:14,350
Say it one more time, handsome.

172
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:15,750
Who am I?

173
00:16:16,960 --> 00:16:19,230
The most beautiful woman in the world.

174
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:21,310
And that's the truth.

175
00:16:21,390 --> 00:16:22,700
Slut.

176
00:16:24,020 --> 00:16:25,320
Prince Doran,

177
00:16:25,590 --> 00:16:27,510
Ser Bronn of the Blackwater.

178
00:16:28,230 --> 00:16:31,340
I didn't realize there were knights of the Blackwater.

179
00:16:31,630 --> 00:16:32,800
Only the one.

180
00:16:32,800 --> 00:16:35,490
I believe you've already met Prince Trystane.

181
00:16:36,230 --> 00:16:37,300
Prince.

182
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,470
Sorry about the other day.

183
00:16:39,560 --> 00:16:41,820
Prince Trystane here is a man of mercy.

184
00:16:41,940 --> 00:16:44,270
He's agreed to grant you your freedom.

185
00:16:46,050 --> 00:16:47,420
I'm glad to hear it.

186
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:51,030
Pie looks good.

187
00:16:51,030 --> 00:16:53,580
There was one condition.

188
00:17:02,810 --> 00:17:04,650
Perhaps some soup instead.

189
00:17:07,540 --> 00:17:10,130
Oysters, clams, and cockles.

190
00:17:12,010 --> 00:17:14,810
Oysters, clams, and cockles.

191
00:17:15,830 --> 00:17:18,570
Oysters, clams, and cockles.

192
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:21,580
Oysters, clams, and cock--

193
00:17:21,580 --> 00:17:23,300
How much for your little clam?

194
00:17:31,770 --> 00:17:34,330
Oysters, clams, and cockles.

195
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:40,270
Oysters, clams, and cockles.

196
00:18:08,290 --> 00:18:09,360
Come on.

197
00:18:12,460 --> 00:18:14,120
Some oysters, girl!

198
00:18:15,370 --> 00:18:17,190
I'm talking to you.

199
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:19,230
Is, uh...

200
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:24,180
- Girl! - Tie her up!

201
00:18:24,420 --> 00:18:26,420
Are you deaf? Girl!

202
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:29,580
Girl!

203
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:36,520
My lord.

204
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:41,830
My lord.

205
00:18:42,670 --> 00:18:44,060
Lord Tyrell.

206
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:46,090
On behalf of the Iron Bank,

207
00:18:46,180 --> 00:18:47,720
may I be the first to welcome you

208
00:18:47,720 --> 00:18:50,120
to the Free City of Braavos.

209
00:18:50,120 --> 00:18:51,790
I hope your journey was trouble-free.

210
00:18:51,790 --> 00:18:53,740
A bit of chop the last few days.

211
00:18:53,750 --> 00:18:55,490
Nothing too awful.

212
00:18:55,580 --> 00:18:58,430
Good to see the old chap still guarding the harbor.

213
00:18:58,510 --> 00:19:00,580
And how goes the harvest in the Reach?

214
00:19:00,580 --> 00:19:02,950
Ah, the vintners say this might be

215
00:19:02,950 --> 00:19:06,170
the best year for red grapes in half a century.

216
00:19:06,280 --> 00:19:09,270
If we come to a satisfactory arrangement,

217
00:19:09,270 --> 00:19:13,940
I'll be sure to send a cask of the Arbor's finest your way.

218
00:19:14,220 --> 00:19:16,480
I'm afraid I don't partake.

219
00:19:24,090 --> 00:19:28,380
Some consider usury distasteful, dishonorable.

220
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:30,550
Pure nonsense, of course.

221
00:19:30,550 --> 00:19:32,740
I'm glad we see eye to eye on this matter.

222
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:35,180
Did you know that at one point Maegor the third

223
00:19:35,180 --> 00:19:37,870
tried to outlaw it in the Seven Kingdoms?

224
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:40,510
Wanted to arrest anyone caught charging interest

225
00:19:40,510 --> 00:19:42,810
and cut off both their hands.

226
00:19:42,810 --> 00:19:45,100
Most unfortunate for the glovers.

227
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:47,110
If a man charges no interest on a loan,

228
00:19:47,110 --> 00:19:49,150
then he has nothing to gain and everything to lose,

229
00:19:49,150 --> 00:19:50,760
so why chance it?

230
00:19:50,780 --> 00:19:52,580
Whereas the promise of reward

231
00:19:52,580 --> 00:19:54,260
makes a man willing to gamble.

232
00:19:54,930 --> 00:19:58,520
We are not gamblers here at the Iron Bank, Lord Tyrell.

233
00:19:58,520 --> 00:20:00,970
You are the world's best gamblers.

234
00:20:00,980 --> 00:20:04,840
And all those bets you won built this.

235
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:17,610
We should celebrate.

236
00:20:17,610 --> 00:20:20,190
I'm afraid I still have a good deal of work to do.

237
00:20:20,190 --> 00:20:21,980
Oh, nonsense. Work's over. Do you sing?

238
00:20:21,990 --> 00:20:23,640
- I don't have that gift. - Oh, it's not a gift.

239
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:25,480
It's a skill. Anyone can learn it.

240
00:20:25,490 --> 00:20:29,830
*So give me a kiss by the Long Canal*

241
00:20:29,830 --> 00:20:33,480
*And give me two kisses in Salty Town*

242
00:20:33,610 --> 00:20:38,610
*For we're going to die tomorrow*

243
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:42,100
*The bareheaded beggar, the king with his crown...*

244
00:20:42,360 --> 00:20:44,870
Thought that old shit would never stop singing.

245
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:46,270
Wasn't bad, though.

246
00:20:46,600 --> 00:20:48,900
The Tyrells can all rot in hell.

247
00:20:49,130 --> 00:20:50,750
Treasonous cunts.

248
00:20:51,130 --> 00:20:53,630
They were going to make that boy-fucker Renly king.

249
00:20:54,740 --> 00:20:56,260
This is the place, lads.

250
00:20:57,060 --> 00:20:59,370
The sleekest little minks in Braavos.

251
00:20:59,520 --> 00:21:01,750
- You buying? - Oh, I'm buying.

252
00:21:02,150 --> 00:21:04,110
But I never was good at sharing.

253
00:21:25,210 --> 00:21:27,370
Sell your fish somewhere else.

254
00:21:27,370 --> 00:21:30,450
Oh, let her in, Brusco. I'm hungry.

255
00:21:31,120 --> 00:21:32,660
Come here, sweetness.

256
00:21:36,540 --> 00:21:39,590
They say oysters get the juices flowing.

257
00:21:39,610 --> 00:21:41,650
We'll take half a dozen.

258
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:44,700
Three coppers.

259
00:21:46,100 --> 00:21:49,100
Here's a silver because the lady likes you.

260
00:22:15,230 --> 00:22:16,400
Too old.

261
00:22:20,520 --> 00:22:21,450
Brea.

262
00:22:36,760 --> 00:22:38,150
Too old.

263
00:22:40,240 --> 00:22:43,590
I have just the one. Anara.

264
00:22:44,980 --> 00:22:47,290
Our most expensive girl.

265
00:22:48,170 --> 00:22:51,200
But well worth it, I assure you.

266
00:22:56,440 --> 00:22:57,930
Too old.

267
00:23:06,030 --> 00:23:08,050
Do you have what I want or not?

268
00:23:08,280 --> 00:23:11,220
Of course. Of course.

269
00:23:17,730 --> 00:23:18,970
These fresh?

270
00:23:23,160 --> 00:23:25,760
Come on, the lads are hungry.

271
00:23:29,230 --> 00:23:32,680
Nothing better for your cockstand than fresh oysters.

272
00:23:34,180 --> 00:23:35,390
- Thank you. - I'll have one.

273
00:23:37,090 --> 00:23:38,240
Any vinegar?

274
00:23:39,910 --> 00:23:42,070
Who let this girl in? Shoo! Shoo!

275
00:24:02,650 --> 00:24:03,760
Good.

276
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:15,640
I'll tell you when we're done.

277
00:24:21,570 --> 00:24:23,580
You'll have a fresh one for me tomorrow?

278
00:24:24,390 --> 00:24:25,680
Of course.

279
00:24:30,410 --> 00:24:32,080
I'll have you whipped, girl.

280
00:24:32,080 --> 00:24:34,120
Go, go on. Out, out, go.

281
00:24:48,190 --> 00:24:49,670
Valar morghulis.

282
00:25:05,790 --> 00:25:06,750
And?

283
00:25:07,570 --> 00:25:09,300
The thin man wasn't hungry today.

284
00:25:09,710 --> 00:25:11,760
Perhaps that is why a man is thin.

285
00:25:12,860 --> 00:25:13,920
Tomorrow.

286
00:25:14,050 --> 00:25:15,140
Tomorrow.

287
00:25:18,220 --> 00:25:19,600
A girl has work to do.

288
00:25:33,500 --> 00:25:35,330
Your rebellion is over.

289
00:25:37,560 --> 00:25:39,880
You can swear your allegiance to me now...

290
00:25:41,300 --> 00:25:42,600
or you can die.

291
00:26:18,330 --> 00:26:20,300
I believe in second chances.

292
00:26:22,680 --> 00:26:25,100
I don't believe in third chances.

293
00:26:53,650 --> 00:26:55,390
You write like a seven-year-old.

294
00:26:56,710 --> 00:26:59,360
Your maester kindly agreed to copy it over for me.

295
00:26:59,360 --> 00:27:00,880
He didn't try to make you pay?

296
00:27:02,980 --> 00:27:04,440
Maybe he's changed.

297
00:27:05,580 --> 00:27:08,300
The queen will be thrilled to know you're bringing her daughter home.

298
00:27:08,530 --> 00:27:09,660
She will.

299
00:27:10,090 --> 00:27:11,890
You love her very much, don't you?

300
00:27:12,080 --> 00:27:13,870
Of course, she's my niece.

301
00:27:14,700 --> 00:27:16,340
I wasn't talking about her.

302
00:27:18,410 --> 00:27:20,250
You think I disapprove.

303
00:27:20,790 --> 00:27:21,910
Why?

304
00:27:22,360 --> 00:27:25,220
Because people disapprove of that sort of thing where you are from?

305
00:27:25,230 --> 00:27:27,860
They disapproved of Oberyn and me where you are from.

306
00:27:28,580 --> 00:27:32,140
Here no one blinked an eye.

307
00:27:33,310 --> 00:27:34,600
100 years ago,

308
00:27:34,600 --> 00:27:36,480
no one would have blinked an eye at you

309
00:27:37,430 --> 00:27:39,520
if you'd been named Targaryen.

310
00:27:40,990 --> 00:27:42,240
It's always changing,

311
00:27:42,240 --> 00:27:45,110
who we're supposed to love and who we're not.

312
00:27:46,420 --> 00:27:48,360
The only thing that stays the same

313
00:27:48,780 --> 00:27:50,940
is that we want who we want.

314
00:28:00,980 --> 00:28:03,270
I know your daughter had no part in the terrible thing

315
00:28:03,270 --> 00:28:05,380
that happened to the man I love.

316
00:28:08,420 --> 00:28:10,630
Perhaps even you are innocent of that.

317
00:28:29,320 --> 00:28:30,290
Father.

318
00:28:34,960 --> 00:28:36,210
Aren't you cold?

319
00:28:38,440 --> 00:28:40,490
No. What are you reading?

320
00:28:41,480 --> 00:28:44,370
- "The Dance of Dragons." - What's it about?

321
00:28:44,370 --> 00:28:46,800
It's the story of the fight between Rhaenyra Targaryen

322
00:28:46,810 --> 00:28:49,720
and her half-brother Aegon for control over the Seven Kingdoms.

323
00:28:50,420 --> 00:28:52,700
Both of them thought they belonged on the Iron Throne.

324
00:28:53,410 --> 00:28:55,980
When people started declaring for one of them or the other,

325
00:28:56,010 --> 00:28:58,210
their fight divided the kingdoms in two.

326
00:28:58,480 --> 00:29:01,560
Brothers fought brothers, dragons fought dragons.

327
00:29:03,360 --> 00:29:06,740
By the time it was over, thousands were dead.

328
00:29:07,790 --> 00:29:10,420
And it was a disaster for the Targaryens as well.

329
00:29:10,700 --> 00:29:12,450
They never truly recovered.

330
00:29:13,390 --> 00:29:14,970
"The Dance of Dragons."

331
00:29:17,210 --> 00:29:18,620
Why is that a dance?

332
00:29:19,480 --> 00:29:20,890
It's just what they call it.

333
00:29:21,270 --> 00:29:22,620
Doesn't make much sense.

334
00:29:23,040 --> 00:29:24,390
I think it's poetic.

335
00:29:31,270 --> 00:29:32,710
If you had to choose

336
00:29:34,380 --> 00:29:37,570
between Rhaenyra and Aegon...

337
00:29:39,360 --> 00:29:40,630
who would you have chosen?

338
00:29:41,170 --> 00:29:42,700
I wouldn't have chosen either.

339
00:29:43,890 --> 00:29:46,380
It's all the choosing sides that made everything so horrible.

340
00:29:46,490 --> 00:29:48,350
Sometimes a person has to choose.

341
00:29:50,800 --> 00:29:54,070
Sometimes the world forces his hand.

342
00:29:56,070 --> 00:29:59,040
If a man knows what he is...

343
00:30:00,380 --> 00:30:03,010
and remains true to himself...

344
00:30:06,700 --> 00:30:08,410
the choice is no choice at all.

345
00:30:09,430 --> 00:30:11,370
He must fulfill his destiny...

346
00:30:14,260 --> 00:30:17,550
and become who he is meant to be.

347
00:30:19,990 --> 00:30:21,970
However much he may hate it.

348
00:30:23,540 --> 00:30:24,990
It's all right, Father.

349
00:30:26,670 --> 00:30:28,690
You don't even know what I'm talking about.

350
00:30:29,670 --> 00:30:30,870
It doesn't matter.

351
00:30:31,230 --> 00:30:32,480
I want to help you.

352
00:30:33,710 --> 00:30:35,160
Is there any way I can help?

353
00:30:42,940 --> 00:30:44,210
Yes, there is.

354
00:30:44,550 --> 00:30:45,990
Good. I want to.

355
00:30:49,050 --> 00:30:51,110
I'm the Princess Shireen of House Baratheon.

356
00:30:51,340 --> 00:30:52,650
And I'm your daughter.

357
00:31:07,800 --> 00:31:09,030
Forgive me.

358
00:31:50,940 --> 00:31:53,580
Where's my father? I want to see my father.

359
00:31:53,580 --> 00:31:55,770
It will all be over soon, Princess.

360
00:32:01,220 --> 00:32:02,280
No.

361
00:32:04,450 --> 00:32:05,840
Where's my father?

362
00:32:06,520 --> 00:32:09,220
No, you can't do this. Father, where are you?

363
00:32:09,270 --> 00:32:11,240
Please, let me see my father.

364
00:32:11,480 --> 00:32:13,890
Father, where are you? Don't let her do this.

365
00:32:15,450 --> 00:32:16,720
Please let go!

366
00:32:18,330 --> 00:32:21,450
Let me see my father! Where are you? Please!

367
00:32:22,620 --> 00:32:24,480
- It's what the Lord wants. - No.

368
00:32:24,600 --> 00:32:27,230
- Please! Let go! No! - It's a good thing.

369
00:32:27,230 --> 00:32:29,330
- A great thing. - Stop. Stop!

370
00:32:29,850 --> 00:32:31,450
- Please! - Hear us now, my Lord.

371
00:32:31,450 --> 00:32:34,060
- You can't do this! - For you, we offer up this girl

372
00:32:34,060 --> 00:32:36,800
- Please! - that you may cleanse her with your fire

373
00:32:36,800 --> 00:32:38,810
and that its light may lead our way.

374
00:32:38,810 --> 00:32:41,010
Please! No, please let me see my father.

375
00:32:41,010 --> 00:32:43,010
If we don't act, we'll all starve here.

376
00:32:43,230 --> 00:32:44,290
All of us.

377
00:32:45,250 --> 00:32:46,670
But if we make this sacrifice...

378
00:32:46,670 --> 00:32:49,380
Accept this token of our faith, my Lord,

379
00:32:49,380 --> 00:32:51,400
and lead us from the darkness.

380
00:32:52,200 --> 00:32:54,960
- Lord of Light, show us the way. - Mother!

381
00:32:55,030 --> 00:32:56,610
Mother, please!

382
00:32:58,990 --> 00:33:00,790
Mother, please! Mother!

383
00:33:00,940 --> 00:33:02,390
- Mother! - We can't.

384
00:33:02,430 --> 00:33:03,530
There's no other way.

385
00:33:03,530 --> 00:33:05,030
- She has king's blood. - Please don't do this!

386
00:33:05,030 --> 00:33:06,710
Lord of Light, protect us.

387
00:33:06,710 --> 00:33:07,750
Please! Father, please!

388
00:33:07,760 --> 00:33:10,470
- For the night is dark and full of terrors. - Father, please!

389
00:33:11,470 --> 00:33:12,280
Father!

390
00:33:12,280 --> 00:33:14,460
Father, don't do this! Please!

391
00:33:14,460 --> 00:33:17,910
Mother, no! Please! Please, help!

392
00:33:17,920 --> 00:33:19,540
Don't do this!

393
00:33:20,100 --> 00:33:23,090
Please, Father! Mother, help!

394
00:33:23,170 --> 00:33:26,190
- No. - No, please! Don't do this!

395
00:33:26,190 --> 00:33:28,430
Don't do this, please, Mother!

396
00:33:29,700 --> 00:33:33,150
Please, Mother! Mother, help!

397
00:33:33,550 --> 00:33:36,430
Mother, help! Help!

398
00:33:36,700 --> 00:33:38,770
Please don't do this, Mother!

399
00:33:38,770 --> 00:33:39,870
Please!

400
00:33:40,280 --> 00:33:41,940
Please, Mother! Please!

401
00:33:42,500 --> 00:33:44,860
Please! No!

402
00:33:44,880 --> 00:33:48,380
Please! No!

403
00:34:05,770 --> 00:34:08,670
No!

404
00:34:58,120 --> 00:34:59,260
Where have you been?

405
00:34:59,840 --> 00:35:01,610
Just making sure everything is in order.

406
00:36:32,530 --> 00:36:33,720
They're waiting for you.

407
00:36:35,560 --> 00:36:36,800
Clap your hands.

408
00:37:06,950 --> 00:37:08,340
That one, the smaller man.

409
00:37:08,340 --> 00:37:10,150
No question, that's where you should put your money.

410
00:37:10,150 --> 00:37:11,380
The smaller man it is.

411
00:37:11,380 --> 00:37:13,340
I'm not putting my money anywhere.

412
00:37:13,340 --> 00:37:15,450
Kings and queens never bet on the games.

413
00:37:15,720 --> 00:37:17,670
Perhaps you should go find someone who does.

414
00:37:18,320 --> 00:37:21,000
People used to bet against me when I fought in the pits.

415
00:37:21,190 --> 00:37:23,910
He would have bet against me. Common novice mistake.

416
00:37:23,910 --> 00:37:25,710
I've spent much of my life in this arena.

417
00:37:25,720 --> 00:37:28,160
And in my experience, large men do triumph

418
00:37:28,160 --> 00:37:30,230
over smaller men far more often than not.

419
00:37:30,240 --> 00:37:33,200
Has your experience ever involved any actual fighting?

420
00:37:33,580 --> 00:37:35,170
You yourself?

421
00:37:35,170 --> 00:37:36,540
Have you ever tried to kill another man

422
00:37:36,540 --> 00:37:38,020
who was trying to kill you?

423
00:37:40,060 --> 00:37:43,080
Whenever I got into the pit against a beast like that one,

424
00:37:43,090 --> 00:37:45,910
the crowd saw me, all skin and bone back then,

425
00:37:45,920 --> 00:37:49,030
then they saw a pile of angry muscles ready to murder me.

426
00:37:49,090 --> 00:37:51,260
They couldn't get their money out fast enough.

427
00:37:51,270 --> 00:37:54,570
But the pile of angry muscles never had any muscles here

428
00:37:54,740 --> 00:37:57,600
or... here.

429
00:37:58,240 --> 00:37:59,830
And the big men were always too slow

430
00:37:59,830 --> 00:38:02,850
to stop my dagger from going where their muscles weren't.

431
00:38:02,850 --> 00:38:06,460
Yes, whenever I saw a beast like that one standing across from me

432
00:38:06,460 --> 00:38:10,200
making his beast faces, I knew I could rest easy.

433
00:38:22,730 --> 00:38:24,090
You don't approve?

434
00:38:24,210 --> 00:38:27,360
There's always been more than enough death in the world for my taste.

435
00:38:27,360 --> 00:38:29,520
I can do without it in my leisure time.

436
00:38:29,520 --> 00:38:32,220
Fair enough. Yet it's an unpleasant question,

437
00:38:32,220 --> 00:38:34,050
but what great thing has ever been accomplished

438
00:38:34,050 --> 00:38:35,850
without killing or cruelty?

439
00:38:35,930 --> 00:38:39,620
It's easy to confuse what is with what ought to be,

440
00:38:39,620 --> 00:38:42,400
especially when what is has worked out in your favor.

441
00:38:42,400 --> 00:38:43,970
I'm not talking about myself.

442
00:38:44,200 --> 00:38:46,800
I'm talking about the necessary conditions for greatness.

443
00:38:46,800 --> 00:38:48,970
That is greatness?

444
00:38:49,080 --> 00:38:52,730
That is a vital part of the great city of Meereen,

445
00:38:52,870 --> 00:38:55,040
which existed long before you or I

446
00:38:55,180 --> 00:38:58,500
and will remain standing long after we have returned to the dirt.

447
00:38:59,590 --> 00:39:01,730
My father would have liked you.

448
00:39:13,460 --> 00:39:16,250
One day your great city will return to the dirt as well.

449
00:39:16,250 --> 00:39:18,170
- At your command? - If need be.

450
00:39:24,660 --> 00:39:27,050
And how many people will die to make this happen?

451
00:39:27,050 --> 00:39:30,260
If it comes to that, they will have died for a good reason.

452
00:39:30,260 --> 00:39:32,230
Those men think they're dying for a good reason.

453
00:39:32,230 --> 00:39:33,690
Someone else's reason.

454
00:39:34,110 --> 00:39:36,350
So your reasons are true and theirs are false?

455
00:39:36,820 --> 00:39:38,920
They don't know their own minds, but you do?

456
00:39:39,350 --> 00:39:41,830
Well said. You're an eloquent man.

457
00:39:42,430 --> 00:39:43,720
Doesn't mean you're wrong.

458
00:39:44,200 --> 00:39:46,340
In my experience, eloquent men are right

459
00:39:46,340 --> 00:39:48,410
every bit as often as imbeciles.

460
00:40:15,730 --> 00:40:17,570
- Your Grace-- - Shut your mouth.

461
00:42:44,980 --> 00:42:46,880
- You can end this. - She cannot.

462
00:42:46,880 --> 00:42:47,680
You can.

463
00:44:26,830 --> 00:44:28,170
Protect your queen!

464
00:44:40,120 --> 00:44:40,960
Go!

465
00:45:06,320 --> 00:45:07,880
Your Grace! Your Grace!

466
00:45:07,880 --> 00:45:09,210
Come with me. I know a way out.

467
00:45:09,210 --> 00:45:10,210
I know a way--

468
00:45:46,720 --> 00:45:47,860
Stay close.

469
00:45:55,330 --> 00:45:56,300
This way.

470
00:46:08,320 --> 00:46:09,810
The other side. Follow me.

471
00:46:13,600 --> 00:46:14,910
Protect your queen!

472
00:49:09,420 --> 00:49:10,690
Drogon!

473
00:50:13,580 --> 00:50:14,690
Valahd.

